?><!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow"><title>Cloud Readiness - Healthcare Wellness Club</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/dashboard.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/step10.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/product_pro.css"></head><body><header class="os-topbar"><div class="os-topbar-inner"><a class="os-brand" href="backup_center.php"><img src="../img/logo.png" alt="logo"><span><strong>Healthcare Wellness Club</strong><small>STEP 18 • Cloud & Production Readiness</small></span></a><div class="os-top-actions"><a class="os-btn" href="backup_policy.php">Policy</a><a class="os-btn" href="disaster_recovery.php">Recovery</a><a class="os-btn primary" href="backup_center.php">Backup Center</a></div></div></header><div class="os-layout"><aside class="os-sidebar"><div class="os-nav-label">Deployment</div><nav class="os-nav"><a href="backup_center.php"><i class="dot"></i>Backup Center</a><a href="backup_policy.php"><i class="dot"></i>Backup Policy</a><a href="disaster_recovery.php"><i class="dot"></i>Recovery Runbook</a><a class="active" href="cloud_readiness.php"><i class="dot"></i>Cloud Readiness</a><a href="step18_audit.php"><i class="dot"></i>STEP 18 Audit</a></nav></aside><main class="os-main"><section class="os-hero s10-hero"><div class="os-kicker">LOCAL NOW • PRODUCTION SAFE LATER</div><h1>Keep local development convenient without confusing it with production security.</h1><p>Cloud readiness evaluates transport, database secrets, backup storage, scheduler policy and recovery requirements. Local XAMPP exceptions are explicitly labelled rather than silently treated as production-safe.</p><div class="os-status-row"><span class="os-chip <?= $local?'':'good' ?>"><?= $local?'LOCAL DEVELOPMENT':'PRODUCTION-LIKE HOST' ?></span><span class="os-chip <?= !empty($runtime['https'])?'good':'' ?>"><?= !empty($runtime['https'])?'HTTPS':'HTTP' ?></span><span class="os-chip"><?= number_format((float)($runtime['db_bytes']??0)/1048576,1) ?> MB DB</span></div></section><?php if($error):?><div class="pp-alert bad"><strong>Cloud diagnostic:</strong> <?= backup_step18_h($error) ?></div><?php else:?><section class="s10-grid" style="margin-top:14px"><article class="s10-card s10-span-8"><h2>Environment Readiness</h2><div class="s10-checks"><?php foreach($checks as $c):?><div class="s10-check <?= $c[2]?'good':'warn' ?>"><div><b><?= backup_step18_h($c[0]) ?></b><span><?= backup_step18_h($c[1]) ?></span></div><strong><?= $c[2]?'PASS':'ACTION' ?></strong></div><?php endforeach;?></div></article><aside class="s10-card s10-span-4"><h2>Production Minimum</h2><div class="s10-list"><div class="s10-row"><div><b>HTTPS only</b><small>TLS certificate and secure cookies.</small></div></div><div class="s10-row"><div><b>Restricted DB user</b><small>No production root account.</small></div></div><div class="s10-row"><div><b>Secrets outside Git</b><small>DB_PASS, setup key, backup passphrase and cloud credentials in environment/secret manager.</small></div></div><div class="s10-row"><div><b>Off-site backup</b><small>At least one encrypted recovery copy outside the application server.</small></div></div><div class="s10-row"><div><b>Provider snapshot</b><small>Use managed database snapshots/native export in addition to portable app backup at larger scale.</small></div></div></div></aside></section><section class="os-card" style="margin-top:14px"><h2>Cloud Backup Adapter Boundary</h2><p>STEP 18 deliberately does not hard-code AWS, Google Cloud, Azure, Dropbox or Drive credentials into the project. The encrypted <code>.hwcbak</code> package is provider-neutral. A future cloud adapter can upload that already-encrypted package without learning its passphrase.</p><p><b>Recommended production pattern:</b> scheduled encrypted portable backup + provider-native managed database backup + off-site retention + periodic restore drill.</p></section><?php endif;?></main></div><script src="assets/business-collapsible.js?v=20260820-1" defer></script></body></html>
